# Chordify

> Chordify is an interactive music learning platform that helps users of all skill levels play along with their favorite songs. It offers synchronized chord diagrams for guitar, piano, ukulele, and mandolin, alongside educational content and song collections.

Chordify provides real-time chord diagrams for millions of songs. These pages are central to the platform and help users learn chords visually and interactively.

## Song pages: `https://chordify.net/chords/[artist-slug]-songs/[recording-slug]-chords`

Example: [Taylor Swift - Love Story](https://chordify.net/chords/taylor-swift-songs/love-story-chords)

These pages include:

- Chord diagram for multiple instruments: guitar, piano, ukulele, mandolin
- Chords over lyrics
- Chord diagrams synced to music playback
- Transposition and tempo control features
- Capo features
- Interactive player to play along
- Song sections: intro, verse etc
- Editor to adjust chords and chord position in the song

Notes:

- English-language content is located at the root level, but we also support French, Polish, Dutch, German, Portuguese, Spanish.
- Chordify content is updated frequently to reflect song releases and learning demand.

## Artist Pages

Artist pages use the format `https://chordify.net/chords/[artist-slug]-songs`. Each artist page includes:

- A curated list of all chordified songs by the artist
- Links to song detail pages
- Setlists the artist appears in
- [Bruno Mars songs](https://chordify.net/chords/bruno-mars-songs): example of an artist page.

## Toolkit

Chordify's toolkit features practice tools that help users train chords, tune their instrument, and keep time.

- [Toolkit](https://chordify.net/toolkit): overview of all practice tools.
- [Chord trainer](https://chordify.net/toolkit/chord-trainer): practice chord shapes and changes.
- [Online guitar tuner](https://chordify.net/toolkit/online-guitar-tuner): tune a guitar with the microphone.
- [Metronome](https://chordify.net/toolkit/metronome): keep time while practicing.
- [Live chord detection](https://chordify.net/toolkit/live-chord-detection): detect the chords that a user plays.

